  <article class="shell journal"><span class="eyebrow">Studio journal / 01 · October 2026</span><h1>What should I make?</h1><p class="journal-lead">A question to carry around for a while.</p><div class="prose"><p>I’m currently working through STUDIO WORKS, an experimental studio incubator for artists and creative technologists developing meaningful, commercially viable objects.</p><p>Over ten weeks, we move from idea to prototype to production and sale. This week begins with a question: what should I make?</p><p>I’m looking back through the things I’ve already made. The light built from a found post. The printed pages. The tools for exploring skateboarding’s history. Which ideas still have energy? Which ones would I want to keep making?</p><p>For now, the work is to notice what keeps coming back.</p><p><a href="https://tiat.dfos.com/">More about STUDIO WORKS ↗</a></p></div><a class="text-link" href="/notes">← All notes</a></article>
